<title>UK: GrandMet/Brown-Forman drop Asda writ.</title>
<headline>GrandMet/Brown-Forman drop Asda writ.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>British drinks group Grand Metropolitan Plc and Brown-Forman Corp said on Friday they have agreed to halt legal action against British supermarket chain Asda Plc.  </p>
<p>GrandMet's International Distillers and Vintners unit and U.S. company Brown-Forman filed the legal action in December 1996, alleging that four of the supermarkets own brands could be mistaken for GrandMet's branded equivalent.</p>
<p>The companies said in a joint statement they had dropped the legal action in exchange for a set of packaging modifications on Asda's own label spirits sold under the names Daniel Boone's, Deep South, ASDA Peach Schnapps and Windward.</p>
<p>The packaging changes will be implemented by ASDA over the next few months.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
